CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ braced default member initializer of scalar: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^Reason:
--
N5008 [dcl.init.list]/3.9: list-initializing a scalar from a single-element
braced-init-list initializes it from that element, so `int x{42};` as a default
member initializer sets the member to 42.  CBMC previously left the
braced-init-list unconverted for a scalar member's default member initializer;
the raw initializer_list reached GOTO conversion and aborted the bit-vector
flattener (boolbv_widtht::get_entry).

